msgid "API stability"
msgstr "Cobhsaíocht API"

msgid ""
"Django is committed to API stability and forwards-compatibility. In a "
"nutshell, this means that code you develop against a version of Django will "
"continue to work with future releases. You may need to make minor changes "
"when upgrading the version of Django your project uses: see the \"Backwards "
"incompatible changes\" section of the :doc:`release note </releases/index>` "
"for the version or versions to which you are upgrading."
msgstr ""
"Tá Django tiomanta do chobhsaíocht API agus do chomhoiriúnacht chun cinn. Go "
"hachomair, ciallaíonn sé seo go leanfaidh cód a fhorbraíonn tú i gcoinne "
"leagan de Django ag obair le heisiúintí amach anseo. Seans go mbeidh ort "
"mionathruithe a dhéanamh agus an leagan de Django a úsáideann do thionscadal "
"á uasghrádú agat: féach an rannán \"Athruithe Neamh-chomhoiriúnacha Siar\" "
"den :doc:`nóta scaoileadh 1` don leagan nó do na leaganacha a bhfuil tú ag "
"uasghrádú orthu."

msgid ""
"At the same time as making API stability a very high priority, Django is "
"also committed to continual improvement, along with aiming for \"one way to "
"do it\" (eventually) in the APIs we provide. This means that when we "
"discover clearly superior ways to do things, we will deprecate and "
"eventually remove the old ways. Our aim is to provide a modern, dependable "
"web framework of the highest quality that encourages best practices in all "
"projects that use it. By using incremental improvements, we try to avoid "
"both stagnation and large breaking upgrades."
msgstr ""
"Ag an am céanna le cobhsaíocht API a dhéanamh mar thosaíocht an-ard, tá "
"Django tiomanta freisin d'fheabhsú leanúnach, chomh maith le bheith dírithe "
"ar \"bealach amháin chun é a dhéanamh\" (faoi dheireadh) sna APIanna a "
"chuirimid ar fáil. Ciallaíonn sé seo nuair a aimsímid go soiléir bealaí níos "
"fearr chun rudaí a dhéanamh, go ndéanfaimid neamhaird de na seanbhealaí agus "
"ar deireadh thiar thall. Tá sé mar aidhm againn creat gréasáin iontaofa, nua-"
"aimseartha den chaighdeán is airde a sholáthar a spreagann dea-chleachtais i "
"ngach tionscadal a úsáideann é. Trí leas a bhaint as feabhsuithe "
"incriminteacha, déanaimid iarracht marbhántacht agus uasghrádú mór briseadh "
"a sheachaint."

msgid "What \"stable\" means"
msgstr "Cad a chiallaíonn \"cobhsaí\"."

msgid "In this context, stable means:"
msgstr "Sa chomhthéacs seo, ciallaíonn cobhsaí:"

msgid ""
"All the public APIs (everything in this documentation) will not be moved or "
"renamed without providing backwards-compatible aliases."
msgstr ""
"Ní bhogfar nó ní athainmneofar gach API poiblí (gach rud sa doiciméadú seo) "
"gan ailiasanna atá comhoiriúnach ar gcúl a sholáthar."

msgid ""
"If new features are added to these APIs -- which is quite possible -- they "
"will not break or change the meaning of existing methods. In other words, "
"\"stable\" does not (necessarily) mean \"complete.\""
msgstr ""
"Má chuirtear gnéithe nua leis na APIanna seo -- rud is féidir go leor -- ní "
"bhrisfidh siad ná ní athróidh siad brí na modhanna atá ann cheana féin. I "
"bhfocail eile, ní chiallaíonn \"cobhsaí\" (go riachtanas) \"iomlán.\""

msgid ""
"If, for some reason, an API declared stable must be removed or replaced, it "
"will be declared deprecated but will remain in the API for at least two "
"feature releases. Warnings will be issued when the deprecated method is "
"called."
msgstr ""
"Más rud é, ar chúis éigin, go gcaithfear API dearbhaithe cobhsaí a bhaint nó "
"a athsholáthar, dearbhófar go bhfuil sé dímheasta ach fanfaidh sé san API ar "
"feadh dhá eisiúint gné ar a laghad. Eiseofar rabhaidh nuair a ghlaofar an "
"modh dímheasta."

msgid ""
"See :ref:`official-releases` for more details on how Django's version "
"numbering scheme works, and how features will be deprecated."
msgstr ""
"Féach : ref: `oifigiúil-eisiúintí` le haghaidh tuilleadh sonraí ar conas a "
"oibríonn scéim uimhrithe leaganacha Django, agus conas a dhéanfar gnéithe a "
"dhímheas."

msgid ""
"We'll only break backwards compatibility of these APIs without a deprecation "
"process if a bug or security hole makes it completely unavoidable."
msgstr ""
"Ní bhrisfimid ar gcúl comhoiriúnacht na APInna seo gan próiseas dímheasa ach "
"amháin má fhágann fabht nó poll slándála é go hiomlán dosheachanta."

msgid "Stable APIs"
msgstr "APIs Cobhsaí"

msgid ""
"In general, everything covered in the documentation -- with the exception of "
"anything in the :doc:`internals area </internals/index>` is considered "
"stable."
msgstr ""
"Go ginearálta, meastar go bhfuil gach rud atá clúdaithe sa doiciméadú -- cé "
"is moite d'aon rud sa :doc:`limistéar inmheánach </internals/index>` cobhsaí."

msgid "Exceptions"
msgstr "Eisceachtaí"

msgid ""
"There are a few exceptions to this stability and backwards-compatibility "
"promise."
msgstr ""
"Tá roinnt eisceachtaí ann maidir leis an gealltanas cobhsaíochta agus cúl-"
"chomhoiriúnachta seo."

msgid "Security fixes"
msgstr "Ceartúcháin slándála"

msgid ""
"If we become aware of a security problem -- hopefully by someone following "
"our :ref:`security reporting policy <reporting-security-issues>` -- we'll do "
"everything necessary to fix it. This might mean breaking backwards "
"compatibility; security trumps the compatibility guarantee."
msgstr ""
"Má thugaimid faoi deara fadhb slándála -- tá súil againn go ndéanfaidh duine "
"éigin ár :tag:`beartas tuairiscithe slándála <reporting-security-issues>` -- "
"déanfaimid gach rud is gá chun í a réiteach. D’fhéadfadh go gciallódh sé seo "
"comhoiriúnacht a bhriseadh ar gcúl; slándáil trumps an ráthaíocht "
"comhoiriúnachta."

msgid "APIs marked as internal"
msgstr "APIs marcáilte mar inmheánach"

msgid "Certain APIs are explicitly marked as \"internal\" in a couple of ways:"
msgstr ""
"Tá APIanna áirithe marcáilte go sainráite mar “inmheánach” ar chúpla bealach:"

msgid ""
"Some documentation refers to internals and mentions them as such. If the "
"documentation says that something is internal, we reserve the right to "
"change it."
msgstr ""
"Tagraíonn roinnt doiciméadú do inmheánaigh agus luaitear iad mar sin. Má "
"deir an doiciméadú go bhfuil rud éigin inmheánach, coimeádaimid an ceart "
"chun é a athrú."

msgid ""
"Functions, methods, and other objects prefixed by a leading underscore "
"(``_``). This is the standard Python way of indicating that something is "
"private; if any method starts with a single ``_``, it's an internal API."
msgstr ""
"Feidhmeanna, modhanna, agus oibiachtaí eile arna réamhshocrú le príomhscór "
"(``_``). Is é seo an bealach Python caighdeánach a chur in iúl go bhfuil rud "
"éigin príobháideach; má thosaíonn modh ar bith le ``_`` amháin, is API "
"inmheánach é."

msgid "Design philosophies"
msgstr "Fealsúnacht dearadh"

msgid ""
"This document explains some of the fundamental philosophies Django's "
"developers have used in creating the framework. Its goal is to explain the "
"past and guide the future."
msgstr ""
"Míníonn an doiciméad seo cuid de na fealsúnachtaí bunúsacha a d'úsáid "
"forbróirí Django chun an creat a chruthú. Is é an sprioc atá aige ná an t-am "
"atá caite a mhíniú agus an todhchaí a threorú."

msgid "Overall"
msgstr "Foriomlán"

msgid "Loose coupling"
msgstr "Cúplála scaoilte"

msgid ""
"A fundamental goal of Django's stack is `loose coupling and tight "
"cohesion`_. The various layers of the framework shouldn't \"know\" about "
"each other unless absolutely necessary."
msgstr ""
"Sprioc bhunúsach de chruach Django is ea `cúpláil scaoilte agus comhtháthú "
"daingean`_. Níor cheart go mbeadh \"eolas\" ag sraitheanna éagsúla an "
"chreata ar a chéile mura rud é go bhfuil géarghá leis."

msgid ""
"For example, the template system knows nothing about web requests, the "
"database layer knows nothing about data display and the view system doesn't "
"care which template system a programmer uses."
msgstr ""
"Mar shampla, níl aon rud ar eolas ag an gcóras teimpléid faoi iarratais "
"gréasáin, níl aon rud ar eolas ag ciseal an bhunachair shonraí faoi "
"thaispeántas sonraí agus is cuma leis an gcóras amhairc cén córas teimpléid "
"a úsáideann ríomhchláraitheoir."

msgid ""
"Although Django comes with a full stack for convenience, the pieces of the "
"stack are independent of another wherever possible."
msgstr ""
"Cé go dtagann Django le stack iomlán le haghaidh áise, tá píosaí an chruach "
"neamhspleách ar cheann eile nuair is féidir."

msgid "Less code"
msgstr "Lúide cód"

msgid ""
"Django apps should use as little code as possible; they should lack "
"boilerplate. Django should take full advantage of Python's dynamic "
"capabilities, such as introspection."
msgstr ""
"Ba cheart go n-úsáidfeadh apps Django chomh beag cód agus is féidir; ba "
"chóir go mbeadh easpa pláta coire orthu. Ba cheart do Django leas iomlán a "
"bhaint as cumais dhinimiciúla Python, mar shampla introspection."

msgid "Quick development"
msgstr "Forbairt tapa"

msgid ""
"The point of a web framework in the 21st century is to make the tedious "
"aspects of web development fast. Django should allow for incredibly quick "
"web development."
msgstr ""
"Is é an pointe a bhaineann le creat gréasáin sa 21ú haois ná na gnéithe "
"tedious d'fhorbairt gréasáin a dhéanamh go tapa. Ba cheart go gceadódh "
"Django forbairt gréasáin thar a bheith gasta."

msgid "Don't repeat yourself (DRY)"
msgstr "Ná déan athrá ort féin (TIRIM)"

msgid ""
"Every distinct concept and/or piece of data should live in one, and only "
"one, place. Redundancy is bad. Normalization is good."
msgstr ""
"Ba cheart go mbeadh gach coincheap agus/nó píosa sonraí ar leith beo in aon "
"áit amháin, agus in áit amháin. Is olc an iomarcaíocht. Tá normalú go maith."

msgid ""
"The framework, within reason, should deduce as much as possible from as "
"little as possible."
msgstr ""
"Ba cheart don chreat, laistigh de chúis, an oiread agus is féidir a bhaint "
"as a laghad agus is féidir."

msgid "The `discussion of DRY on the Portland Pattern Repository`__"
msgstr "An `plé ar an bprionsabal TIRIM ar an Taisclann Patrún Portland`__"

msgid "Explicit is better than implicit"
msgstr "Is fearr soiléir ná intuigthe"

msgid ""
"This is a core Python principle listed in :pep:`20`, and it means Django "
"shouldn't do too much \"magic.\" Magic shouldn't happen unless there's a "
"really good reason for it. Magic is worth using only if it creates a huge "
"convenience unattainable in other ways, and it isn't implemented in a way "
"that confuses developers who are trying to learn how to use the feature."
msgstr ""
"Is prionsabal lárnach Python é seo atá liostaithe i :pep:`20`, agus "
"ciallaíonn sé nár cheart do Django an iomarca \"draíochta.\" Níor cheart go "
"dtarlódh draíocht mura bhfuil cúis mhaith leis. Is fiú draíocht a úsáid ach "
"amháin má chruthaíonn sé áis ollmhór nach féidir a bhaint amach ar bhealaí "
"eile, agus nach gcuirtear i bhfeidhm é ar bhealach a chuireann mearbhall ar "
"fhorbróirí atá ag iarraidh a fháil amach conas an ghné a úsáid."

msgid "Consistency"
msgstr "Comhsheasmhacht"

msgid ""
"The framework should be consistent at all levels. Consistency applies to "
"everything from low-level (the Python coding style used) to high-level (the "
"\"experience\" of using Django)."
msgstr ""
"Ba cheart go mbeadh an creat comhsheasmhach ar gach leibhéal. Baineann "
"comhsheasmhacht le gach rud ó leibhéal íseal (an stíl códaithe Python a "
"úsáidtear) go dtí ardleibhéal (an \"taithí\" ar Django a úsáid)."

msgid "Models"
msgstr "Múnlaí"

msgid ""
"Fields shouldn't assume certain behaviors based solely on the name of the "
"field. This requires too much knowledge of the system and is prone to "
"errors. Instead, behaviors should be based on keyword arguments and, in some "
"cases, on the type of the field."
msgstr ""
"Níor cheart go nglacfadh réimsí le hiompraíochtaí áirithe bunaithe ar ainm "
"na páirce amháin. Éilíonn sé seo an iomarca eolais ar an gcóras agus seans "
"maith go mbeidh earráidí ann. Ina áit sin, ba cheart go mbeadh iompraíochtaí "
"bunaithe ar argóintí eochairfhocail agus, i gcásanna áirithe, ar an gcineál "
"réimse."

msgid "Include all relevant domain logic"
msgstr "Cuir san áireamh gach loighic fearainn ábhartha"

msgid ""
"Models should encapsulate every aspect of an \"object,\" following Martin "
"Fowler's `Active Record`_ design pattern."
msgstr ""
"Ba chóir go gcuimseodh samhlacha gach gné de \"réad,\" ag leanúint patrún "
"dearaidh `Taifead Gníomhach`_ Martin Fowler."

msgid ""
"This is why both the data represented by a model and information about it "
"(its human-readable name, options like default ordering, etc.) are defined "
"in the model class; all the information needed to understand a given model "
"should be stored *in* the model."
msgstr ""
"Sin é an fáth a sainmhínítear na sonraí arna léiriú ag samhail agus faisnéis "
"faoi (a hainm inléite ag an duine, roghanna mar ordú réamhshocraithe, etc.) "
"san aicme mhúnla; ba chóir an fhaisnéis go léir a theastaíonn chun "
"mionsamhail ar leith a thuiscint a stóráil *sa mhionsamhail."

msgid "Database API"
msgstr "Bunachar Sonraí API"

msgid "The core goals of the database API are:"
msgstr "Is iad príomhspriocanna an API bunachar sonraí:"

msgid "SQL efficiency"
msgstr "Éifeachtúlacht SQL"

msgid ""
"It should execute SQL statements as few times as possible, and it should "
"optimize statements internally."
msgstr ""
"Ba cheart dó ráitis SQL a fhorghníomhú chomh beag agus is féidir, agus ba "
"cheart dó ráitis a bharrfheabhsú go hinmheánach."

msgid ""
"This is why developers need to call ``save()`` explicitly, rather than the "
"framework saving things behind the scenes silently."
msgstr ""
"Sin é an fáth gur gá d'fhorbróirí ``save()`` a ghlaoch go sainráite, seachas "
"an creat a shábháil rudaí taobh thiar de na radhairc go ciúin."

msgid ""
"This is also why the ``select_related()`` ``QuerySet`` method exists. It's "
"an optional performance booster for the common case of selecting \"every "
"related object.\""
msgstr ""
"Sin é an fáth freisin go bhfuil an modh ``select_related()```QuerySet`` ann. "
"Is teanndáileog feidhmíochta roghnach é don chás coitianta \"gach rud "
"gaolmhar\" a roghnú."

msgid "Terse, powerful syntax"
msgstr "Terse, comhréir chumhachtach"

msgid ""
"The database API should allow rich, expressive statements in as little "
"syntax as possible. It should not rely on importing other modules or helper "
"objects."
msgstr ""
"Ba cheart go gceadódh API an bhunachair sonraí ráitis shaibhre léiritheacha "
"chomh beag comhréire agus is féidir. Níor cheart go mbeadh sé ag brath ar "
"mhodúil eile nó ar rudaí cabhrach a allmhairiú."

msgid ""
"Joins should be performed automatically, behind the scenes, when necessary."
msgstr ""
"Ba chóir siúntaí a dhéanamh go huathoibríoch, taobh thiar de na radhairc, "
"nuair is gá."

msgid ""
"Every object should be able to access every related object, systemwide. This "
"access should work both ways."
msgstr ""
"Ba cheart go mbeadh gach réad in ann rochtain a fháil ar gach réad gaolmhar, "
"ar fud an chórais. Ba cheart go n-oibreodh an rochtain seo ar an dá bhealach."

msgid "Option to drop into raw SQL easily, when needed"
msgstr "Rogha chun titim isteach i SQL amh go héasca, nuair is gá"

msgid ""
"The database API should realize it's a shortcut but not necessarily an end-"
"all-be-all. The framework should make it easy to write custom SQL -- entire "
"statements, or just custom ``WHERE`` clauses as custom parameters to API "
"calls."
msgstr ""
"Ba cheart go n-aithneodh API an bhunachair sonraí gur aicearra é ach ní gá "
"gur rud deireadh é. Ba cheart go n-éascódh an creat ráitis shaincheaptha SQL "
"-- ráitis iomlána a scríobh, nó clásail saincheaptha `` WHERE`` mar "
"pharaiméadair saincheaptha do ghlaonna API."

msgid "URL design"
msgstr "Dearadh URL"

msgid ""
"URLs in a Django app should not be coupled to the underlying Python code. "
"Tying URLs to Python function names is a Bad And Ugly Thing."
msgstr ""
"Níor cheart URLanna in aip Django a chúpláil leis an mbunchód Python. Rud "
"Droch agus Gránna is ea URLanna a cheangal le hainmneacha feidhm Python."

msgid ""
"Along these lines, the Django URL system should allow URLs for the same app "
"to be different in different contexts. For example, one site may put stories "
"at ``/stories/``, while another may use ``/news/``."
msgstr ""
"Mar an gcéanna, ba cheart go gceadódh córas URL Django URLanna don app "
"céanna a bheith difriúil i gcomhthéacsanna éagsúla. Mar shampla, féadfaidh "
"suíomh amháin scéalta a chur ag ``/scéalta/``, agus féadfaidh suíomh eile ``/"
"nuacht/`` a úsáid."

msgid "Infinite flexibility"
msgstr "Solúbthacht gan teorainn"

msgid ""
"URLs should be as flexible as possible. Any conceivable URL design should be "
"allowed."
msgstr ""
"Ba cheart go mbeadh URLanna chomh solúbtha agus is féidir. Ba cheart aon "
"dearadh URL infhaighte a cheadú."

msgid "Encourage best practices"
msgstr "Spreag na cleachtais is fearr"

msgid ""
"The framework should make it just as easy (or even easier) for a developer "
"to design pretty URLs than ugly ones."
msgstr ""
"Ba cheart go ndéanfadh an creat é chomh héasca (nó níos fusa fós) "
"d’fhorbróir URLanna áille a dhearadh ná na cinn ghránna."

msgid "File extensions in web-page URLs should be avoided."
msgstr "Ba cheart síntí comhaid i URLanna leathanaigh ghréasáin a sheachaint."

msgid "Vignette-style commas in URLs deserve severe punishment."
msgstr "Tá pionós trom tuillte ag camóga ar nós vignette i URLanna."

msgid "Definitive URLs"
msgstr "URLanna cinntitheacha"

msgid ""
"Technically, ``foo.com/bar`` and ``foo.com/bar/`` are two different URLs, "
"and search-engine robots (and some web traffic-analyzing tools) would treat "
"them as separate pages. Django should make an effort to \"normalize\" URLs "
"so that search-engine robots don't get confused."
msgstr ""
"Go teicniúil, is dhá URL dhifriúla iad `` foo.com/bar`` agus `` foo.com/bar/"
"``, agus déileálfadh róbait inneall cuardaigh (agus roinnt uirlisí anailíse "
"tráchta gréasáin) leo mar leathanaigh ar leith. Ba cheart do Django iarracht "
"a dhéanamh URLanna a \"normalú\" ionas nach gcuirfí mearbhall ar róbait "
"inneall cuardaigh."

msgid "This is the reasoning behind the :setting:`APPEND_SLASH` setting."
msgstr "Seo é an réasúnaíocht taobh thiar den socrú :setting:`APPEND_SLASH`."

msgid "Template system"
msgstr "Córas teimpléad"

msgid "Separate logic from presentation"
msgstr "Loighic a scaradh ón gcur i láthair"

msgid ""
"We see a template system as a tool that controls presentation and "
"presentation-related logic -- and that's it. The template system shouldn't "
"support functionality that goes beyond this basic goal."
msgstr ""
"Feicimid córas teimpléid mar uirlis a rialaíonn cur i láthair agus loighic a "
"bhaineann le cur i láthair -- agus sin é. Níor cheart go dtacódh an córas "
"teimpléad le feidhmiúlacht a théann thar an mbunsprioc seo."

msgid "Discourage redundancy"
msgstr "Díspreagadh iomarcaíocht"

msgid ""
"The majority of dynamic websites use some sort of common sitewide design -- "
"a common header, footer, navigation bar, etc. The Django template system "
"should make it easy to store those elements in a single place, eliminating "
"duplicate code."
msgstr ""
"Úsáideann formhór na suíomhanna gréasáin dinimiciúla dearadh comónta ar fud "
"an tsuímh de shaghas éigin - ceanntásc coiteann, buntásc, barra nascleanúna, "
"etc. Ba cheart go n-éascódh córas teimpléid Django na heilimintí sin a "
"stóráil in aon áit amháin, rud a chuirfeadh deireadh le cód dúblach."

msgid ""
"This is the philosophy behind :ref:`template inheritance <template-"
"inheritance>`."
msgstr ""
"Seo í an fhealsúnacht taobh thiar de :tag:`oidhreacht teimpléad <template-"
"inheritance>`."

msgid "Be decoupled from HTML"
msgstr "Déan é a dhíchúpláil ó HTML"

msgid ""
"The template system shouldn't be designed so that it only outputs HTML. It "
"should be equally good at generating other text-based formats, or just plain "
"text."
msgstr ""
"Níor cheart an córas teimpléid a dhearadh sa chaoi is nach n-aschuireann sé "
"ach HTML. Ba cheart go mbeadh sé chomh maith céanna ag cruthú formáidí téacs-"
"bhunaithe eile, nó gnáth-théacs amháin."

msgid "XML should not be used for template languages"
msgstr "Níor cheart XML a úsáid le haghaidh teangacha teimpléid"

msgid ""
"Using an XML engine to parse templates introduces a whole new world of human "
"error in editing templates -- and incurs an unacceptable level of overhead "
"in template processing."
msgstr ""
"Trí inneall XML a úsáid chun teimpléid a pharsáil, tugtar isteach domhan "
"iomlán nua earráide daonna in eagarthóireacht teimpléid -- agus tabhaítear "
"leibhéal do-ghlactha forchostais i bpróiseáil teimpléad."

msgid "Assume designer competence"
msgstr "Glac leis inniúlacht dearthóir"

msgid ""
"The template system shouldn't be designed so that templates necessarily are "
"displayed nicely in WYSIWYG editors such as Dreamweaver. That is too severe "
"of a limitation and wouldn't allow the syntax to be as nice as it is. Django "
"expects template authors are comfortable editing HTML directly."
msgstr ""
"Níor cheart an córas teimpléid a dhearadh sa chaoi is go dtaispeánfar "
"teimpléid go deas in eagarthóirí WYSIWYG ar nós Dreamweaver. Is teorannú ró-"
"dhian é sin agus ní ligfeadh sé don chomhréir a bheith chomh deas agus atá "
"sé. Tá Django ag súil go mbeidh údair teimpléid compordach ag "
"eagarthóireacht HTML go díreach."

msgid "Treat whitespace obviously"
msgstr "Caitheamh spás bán ar ndóigh"

msgid ""
"The template system shouldn't do magic things with whitespace. If a template "
"includes whitespace, the system should treat the whitespace as it treats "
"text -- just display it. Any whitespace that's not in a template tag should "
"be displayed."
msgstr ""
"Níor cheart don chóras teimpléad rudaí draíochta a dhéanamh le spás bán. Má "
"tá spás bán i dteimpléad, ba cheart go gcaithfeadh an córas leis an spás bán "
"mar a dhéileálann sé le téacs -- ní gá ach é a thaispeáint. Ba cheart spás "
"bán ar bith nach bhfuil i gclib teimpléad a thaispeáint."

msgid "Don't invent a programming language"
msgstr "Ná ceapadh teanga ríomhchlárúcháin"

msgid ""
"The goal is not to invent a programming language. The goal is to offer just "
"enough programming-esque functionality, such as branching and looping, that "
"is essential for making presentation-related decisions. The :ref:`Django "
"Template Language (DTL) <template-language-intro>` aims to avoid advanced "
"logic."
msgstr ""
"Ní hé an sprioc teanga ríomhchlárúcháin a chumadh. Is é an sprioc gan ach go "
"leor feidhmiúlacht ríomhchlárúcháin a thairiscint, mar bhrainse agus lúbadh, "
"atá riachtanach chun cinntí a bhaineann le cur i láthair a dhéanamh. Tá sé "
"mar aidhm ag an :ref:`Teanga Teimpléad Django (DTL) <template-language-"
"intro>` ard-loighic a sheachaint."

msgid "Safety and security"
msgstr "Sábháilteacht agus slándáil"

msgid ""
"The template system, out of the box, should forbid the inclusion of "
"malicious code -- such as commands that delete database records."
msgstr ""
"Ba cheart go gcuirfeadh an córas teimpléad, as an mbosca, cosc ​​ar chód "
"mailíseach a áireamh -- mar orduithe a scriosann taifid bhunachar sonraí."

msgid ""
"This is another reason the template system doesn't allow arbitrary Python "
"code."
msgstr ""
"Is cúis eile é seo nach gceadaíonn an córas teimpléad cód treallach Python."

msgid "Extensibility"
msgstr "Leathnú"

msgid ""
"The template system should recognize that advanced template authors may want "
"to extend its technology."
msgstr ""
"Ba cheart go n-aithneodh an córas teimpléad go mb’fhéidir gur mhaith le "
"húdair ardteimpléid a dteicneolaíocht a leathnú."

msgid "This is the philosophy behind custom template tags and filters."
msgstr ""
"Is é seo an fhealsúnacht taobh thiar de chlibeanna agus scagairí teimpléid "
"saincheaptha."

msgid "Views"
msgstr "Radhairc"

msgid "Simplicity"
msgstr "Simplíocht"

msgid ""
"Writing a view should be as simple as writing a Python function. Developers "
"shouldn't have to instantiate a class when a function will do."
msgstr ""
"Ba chóir go mbeadh scríobh tuairim chomh simplí le feidhm Python a scríobh. "
"Níor cheart go mbeadh ar fhorbróirí rang a chur ar an toirt nuair a "
"dhéanfaidh feidhm."

msgid "Use request objects"
msgstr "Úsáid rudaí iarratais"

msgid ""
"Views should have access to a request object -- an object that stores "
"metadata about the current request. The object should be passed directly to "
"a view function, rather than the view function having to access the request "
"data from a global variable. This makes it light, clean and easy to test "
"views by passing in \"fake\" request objects."
msgstr ""
"Ba cheart go mbeadh rochtain ag radhairc ar oibiacht iarratais -- réad a "
"stórálann meiteashonraí faoin iarratas reatha. Ba cheart an réad a chur ar "
"aghaidh go díreach chuig feidhm amhairc, seachas go mbeadh ar an bhfeidhm "
"radhairc rochtain a fháil ar shonraí an iarratais ó athróg dhomhanda. Fágann "
"sé seo go bhfuil sé éadrom, glan agus éasca le tuairimí a thástáil trí rudaí "
"iarratais \"falsa\" a chur isteach."

msgid ""
"A view shouldn't care about which template system the developer uses -- or "
"even whether a template system is used at all."
msgstr ""
"Níor cheart go mbeadh cuma ar an tuairim cén córas teimpléid a úsáideann an "
"forbróir -- nó fiú an n-úsáidtear córas teimpléid ar chor ar bith."

msgid "Differentiate between GET and POST"
msgstr "Déan idirdhealú idir GET agus POST"

msgid ""
"GET and POST are distinct; developers should explicitly use one or the "
"other. The framework should make it easy to distinguish between GET and POST "
"data."
msgstr ""
"tá GET agus POST ar leith; ba cheart d'fhorbróirí ceann amháin nó an ceann "
"eile a úsáid go sainráite. Ba cheart go n-éascódh an creat idirdhealú a "
"dhéanamh idir sonraí GET agus POST."

msgid "Cache Framework"
msgstr "Chreat Cache"

msgid "The core goals of Django's :doc:`cache framework </topics/cache>` are:"
msgstr "Is iad príomhspriocanna Django's :doc:`creat taisce </topics/cache>`:"

msgid ""
"A cache should be as fast as possible.  Hence, all framework code "
"surrounding the cache backend should be kept to the absolute minimum, "
"especially for ``get()`` operations."
msgstr ""
"Ba chóir go mbeadh taisce chomh tapa agus is féidir. Mar sin, ba cheart an "
"creatchód ar fad a bhaineann leis an inneall taisce a choinneáil chomh "
"híseal agus is féidir, go háirithe le haghaidh oibríochtaí ``get()``."

msgid ""
"The cache API should provide a consistent interface across the different "
"cache backends."
msgstr ""
"Ba cheart go soláthródh an API taisce comhéadan comhsheasmhach thar na "
"haiséilí éagsúla taisce."

msgid ""
"The cache API should be extensible at the application level based on the "
"developer's needs (for example, see :ref:`cache_key_transformation`)."
msgstr ""
"Ba cheart go mbeadh an API taisce insínte ag leibhéal an fheidhmchláir "
"bunaithe ar riachtanais an fhorbróra (mar shampla, féach : ref: "
"`cache_key_transformation`)."

msgid "Third-party distributions of Django"
msgstr "Dáiltí tríú páirtí Django"

msgid ""
"Many third-party distributors are now providing versions of Django "
"integrated with their package-management systems. These can make "
"installation and upgrading much easier for users of Django since the "
"integration includes the ability to automatically install dependencies (like "
"database adapters) that Django requires."
msgstr ""
"Tá go leor dáileoirí tríú páirtí ag soláthar leaganacha de Django atá "
"comhtháite lena gcórais bhainistíochta pacáiste anois. Is féidir leo seo "
"suiteáil agus uasghrádú a dhéanamh i bhfad níos éasca d'úsáideoirí Django ós "
"rud é go n-áirítear leis an gcomhtháthú an cumas spleáchais a shuiteáil go "
"huathoibríoch (cosúil le hoiriúnóirí bunachar sonraí) a éilíonn Django."

msgid ""
"Typically, these packages are based on the latest stable release of Django, "
"so if you want to use the development version of Django you'll need to "
"follow the instructions for :ref:`installing the development version "
"<installing-development-version>` from our Git repository."
msgstr ""
"De ghnáth, bíonn na pacáistí seo bunaithe ar an scaoileadh cobhsaí is déanaí "
"de Django, mar sin más mian leat an leagan forbartha de Django a úsáid beidh "
"ort na treoracha le haghaidh :ref:`an leagan forbartha <installing-"
"development-version>` a shuiteáil ónár stór Git."

msgid ""
"If you're using Linux or a Unix installation, such as OpenSolaris, check "
"with your distributor to see if they already package Django. If you're using "
"a Linux distro and don't know how to find out if a package is available, "
"then now is a good time to learn.  The Django Wiki contains a list of `Third "
"Party Distributions`_ to help you out."
msgstr ""
"Má tá Linux nó suiteáil Unix á úsáid agat, mar OpenSolaris, seiceáil le do "
"dháileoir féachaint an bhfuil Django á phacáistiú acu cheana féin. Má tá "
"distro Linux á úsáid agat agus nach bhfuil a fhios agat conas a fháil amach "
"an bhfuil pacáiste ar fáil, is tráth maith é anois le foghlaim. Sa Vicí "
"Django tá liosta de `Dáilte Tríú Páirtí`_ chun cabhrú leat."

msgid "For distributors"
msgstr "Do dháileoirí"

msgid ""
"If you'd like to package Django for distribution, we'd be happy to help out! "
"Please introduce yourself on the `Django Forum`_."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"We also encourage all distributors to subscribe to the |django-announce| "
"mailing list, which is a (very) low-traffic list for announcing new releases "
"of Django and important bugfixes."
msgstr ""
"Molaimid freisin do na dáileoirí go léir liostáil don |django-announce| "
"liosta seoltaí, atá ina liosta (an-) tráchta íseal chun eisiúintí nua Django "
"agus ceartúcháin thábhachtacha a fhógairt."

msgid "Meta-documentation and miscellany"
msgstr "Meta-dhoiciméadú agus ilghnéitheacht"

msgid ""
"Documentation that we can't find a more organized place for. Like that "
"drawer in your kitchen with the scissors, batteries, duct tape, and other "
"junk."
msgstr ""
"Doiciméadú nach féidir linn áit níos eagraithe a aimsiú dó. Cosúil leis an "
"tarraiceán sin i do chistin leis na siosúr, na cadhnraí, an téip duct, agus "
"an junk eile."
